 "nodeCategoryNote": "SPECIAL = a neutral vat T4 hotspot (huge garrison, most production), mirrored fair; never a home (Daniele 2026-11-27)",
 "note": "Y-05 Catapult Bay (was G-05): 11 platforms, 13 bridges + 2 joints, decks 3.16-10.84 m, 81 x 56 m. Bay + catapults kept (launchers -> retract relays); centre SPECIAL T4; junction ring dropped.",
 "ruleWaivers": {
  "G05": "3.0: deck lengths off the kit tiers on purpose (joined inside a cluster, long between clusters)",
  "L01": "3.0: the Last Stand is the quota (lastStand.quota), no corner methods",
  "G02": "3.0 clusters: joined platforms touch (joint centre distance 15.5 m < minNodeGap 15)",
  "G03": "3.0 clusters: a joint has no deck (0 m between the rims), so no tier length applies",
  "N05": "3.0 relays: a relay's moving decks are the test",
  "N03": "3.0 WP2b: checked per relay state instead (gmaps3.problems: in EVERY switch / rotation / retract state the homes stay linked); removing both states of a switch at once cannot happen in play",
  "N04": "3.0 WP2b: clusters + longer bridges leave some platforms on one fixed deck and their joints; every relay state keeps the homes linked",
  "N11": "3.0 WP2b: the box at R 7.6 holds short chains (cluster platforms count their joints, not decks)",
  "N12": "3.0 WP2b: 4.x routing guidance (relays on the fastest route); relays are placed by the G map's identity",
  "G09": "3.0 WP2b: the 4.x one-front-door art rule; 3.0 platforms have two doors (Rules.TWO_DOORS) and relay views are WP3's slots3 (flag for WP3)"
 },
